# hinged - allow the daemon to create the synthetic SW_TABLET_MODE device.
#
# /dev/uinput is crw------- root:root by default, so creating a virtual input
# device requires root.
#
# SECURITY, STATED PLAINLY: write access to /dev/uinput is the ability to
# synthesize arbitrary input - including keystrokes - into the active session.
# That is a strictly larger capability than the read access this project
# declines to grant via `usermod -aG input`, so granting it to the whole
# `input` group would be inconsistent. systemd deliberately ships no uinput
# rule at all for this reason.
#
# The preferred arrangement is therefore NOT this file: run the daemon as a
# system service with DeviceAllow=/dev/uinput rw, so the capability belongs to
# one hardened unit rather than to every process a user runs.
#
# This file exists for development and for people who understand the tradeoff.
# uaccess scopes it to the active local session rather than a persistent group,
# which is the lesser of the two evils.
#
# static_node= is required because the uinput module is often not loaded when
# udev processes rules, so there is no device node yet to apply a mode to.

ACTION=="remove", GOTO="hinged_uinput_end"
KERNEL=="uinput", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", TAG+="uaccess", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
LABEL="hinged_uinput_end"
